  "version": "2026-09-14 pass 2",
  "note": "Every number a designer is likely to want to change. js/rules.js applyBalance() folds this onto the other data files at load time, so the engine keeps reading def.cost, recipe.time and so on. Values here are absolute overrides; the *ByCategory / *ByTier tables are multipliers against the shipped numbers. Rules of thumb this file follows: early buildings are cheap and fast so the first twenty minutes are decisions rather than saving up, late buildings are expensive so the endgame is a real project, and there is never less than six minutes of quiet between attacks so there is time to explore and build. Pass 2 (2026-09-14) widened the raw end - drills, pumps and labs - because the balance sim showed ore extraction, not machine count, was what every chain above steel was waiting on, and softened the wave curve so a six-hour run to a rocket is a slope not a cliff.",
